# Cursor AI Rules - RaConnect Laravel Admin Panel
# Best Coding Practices & Standards

## Project Context
This is a multi-tenant CRM system built with Laravel 12, Filament v4, and Stancl/Tenancy.
It's migrating from a legacy Laravel 5.8 system with complex business logic.

---

## 1. PHP & Laravel Standards

### PHP Version & Type Safety
```php
// ALWAYS start files with strict types
declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Models;

// ALWAYS use full type hints
class Order extends Model
{
    // Type hint return types
    public function calculateDebt(): float
    {
        return $this->price_to_customer - $this->getPaidAmount();
    }
    
    // Type hint parameters
    public function assignTo(User $user): void
    {
        $this->user()->associate($user);
        $this->save();
    }
    
    // Type hint relationships
    public function client(): BelongsTo
    {
        return $this->belongsTo(Client::class);
    }
}
```

### Use Modern Laravel Features
```php
// ✅ CORRECT - Use property-based casting (Laravel 12)
protected function casts(): array
{
    return [
        'email_verified_at' => 'datetime',
        'password' => 'hashed',
        'is_active' => 'boolean',
    ];
}

// ❌ WRONG - Old array property
protected $casts = ['is_active' => 'boolean'];

// ✅ CORRECT - Use enums for fixed values (PHP 8.1+)
enum OrderStatus: string
{
    case Requested = 'requested';
    case Confirmed = 'confirmed';
    case Delivered = 'delivered';
    case Finished = 'finished';
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Use readonly properties (PHP 8.1+)
class OrderService
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly OrderRepository $repository,
        private readonly NotificationService $notifier
    ) {}
}
```

### Naming Conventions
```php
// Classes: PascalCase
class OrderCalculationService {}

// Methods: camelCase
