## 2. Multi-Tenancy Rules (CRITICAL)

### NEVER Add tenant_id Fields
```php
// ❌ WRONG - Do NOT add tenant_id to tenant tables
Schema::create('orders', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->id();
    $table->foreignId('tenant_id'); // ❌ NEVER DO THIS
});

// ✅ CORRECT - No tenant_id needed
Schema::create('orders', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->id();
    $table->foreignId('client_id')->constrained();
    // Database switching handles tenant isolation
});
```

### Always Test Tenant Isolation
```php
// ✅ REQUIRED - Test that tenants can't access each other's data
public function test_tenant_cannot_access_other_tenant_orders(): void
{
    $tenant1 = Tenant::factory()->create();
    $tenant2 = Tenant::factory()->create();
    
    tenancy()->initialize($tenant1);
    $order1 = Order::factory()->create();
    
    tenancy()->initialize($tenant2);
    
    // Should not find tenant1's order
    $this->assertDatabaseMissing('orders', ['id' => $order1->id]);
    $this->assertEquals(0, Order::count());
}
```

### Tenant-Aware File Operations
```php
// ✅ CORRECT - Use TenantFileService for file operations
use App\Services\TenantFileService;

public function storeDocument(UploadedFile $file): Document
{
    $service = app(TenantFileService::class);
    $path = $service->store($file, 'documents');
    
    return Document::create([
        'file_name' => $file->getClientOriginalName(),
        'file_path' => $path,
    ]);
}

// ❌ WRONG - Direct file storage without tenant context
Storage::disk('public')->put('documents/' . $file->getClientOriginalName(), $file);
```

