## 5. Service Classes for Business Logic

### Extract Complex Calculations to Services
```php
// ✅ CORRECT - Create service classes for complex operations
// app/Services/OrderFinancialService.php
namespace App\Services;

class OrderFinancialService
{
    public function calculateDebtFromCustomer(Order $order): float
    {
        $totalPrice = $order->price_to_customer;
        $paidAmount = $this->calculatePaidAmount($order);
        
        return max(0, $totalPrice - $paidAmount);
    }
    
    public function calculatePaidAmount(Order $order): float
    {
        return $order->documents()
            ->where('type', 'revenue')
            ->where('is_paid', true)
            ->sum('price');
    }
    
    public function calculateBalance(Order $order): float
    {
        return $this->calculateDebtFromCustomer($order) 
             - $this->calculateDebtToSupplier($order);
    }
}

// Use in controller/resource
$financialService = app(OrderFinancialService::class);
$debt = $financialService->calculateDebtFromCustomer($order);
```

