## 6. Database & Query Optimization

### Always Eager Load Relationships
```php
// ✅ CORRECT - Eager load to avoid N+1
$orders = Order::with([
    'client.company',
    'place',
    'articles',
    'documents',
    'user',
])->paginate(50);

// ❌ WRONG - N+1 query problem
$orders = Order::paginate(50);
foreach ($orders as $order) {
    echo $order->client->name; // N queries!
}
```

### Use Database Transactions
```php
// ✅ CORRECT - Wrap related operations in transaction
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\DB;

public function finishOrder(Order $order): void
{
    DB::transaction(function () use ($order) {
        $order->update(['is_finished' => true]);
        $order->montages()->update(['confirmed' => true]);
        $order->articles()->detach();
        
        event(new OrderFinished($order));
    });
}
```

### Add Indexes for Performance
```php
// ✅ CORRECT - Index frequently queried columns
Schema::create('orders', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->id();
    $table->string('number');
    $table->foreignId('client_id')->constrained();
    
    // Add indexes
    $table->index('number');
    $table->index('install_date');
    $table->index(['client_id', 'is_finished']);
});
```

