## 10. Documentation Standards

### Document Complex Business Logic
```php
/**
 * Calculate the total montage time required for this order.
 * 
 * This sums the montage time for all articles attached to the order,
 * taking into account the quantity of each article.
 * 
 * Formula: SUM(article.quantity × article.montage_time)
 * 
 * @return float Total hours required
 */
protected function montageTime(): Attribute
{
    return Attribute::make(
        get: fn () => $this->articles->sum(fn ($article) => 
            $article->pivot->quantity * $article->pivot->montage_time
        ),
    );
}
```

### Use Type Hints Instead of PHPDoc Where Possible
```php
// ✅ CORRECT - Type hints are self-documenting
public function calculateDebt(Order $order): float
{
    return $this->total - $this->paid;
}

// ❌ WRONG - Unnecessary PHPDoc when types are clear
/**
 * @param Order $order
 * @return float
 */
public function calculateDebt($order)
{
    return $this->total - $this->paid;
}
```

