## 11. Error Handling

### Use Exceptions for Business Logic Errors
```php
// ✅ CORRECT - Custom exceptions
namespace App\Exceptions;

class OrderCannotBeFinishedException extends \Exception
{
    public static function notAllArticlesDelivered(Order $order): self
    {
        return new self(
            "Order {$order->number} cannot be finished: not all articles are delivered."
        );
    }
}

// Use in service
public function finishOrder(Order $order): void
{
    if (!$order->articles->every->pivot->is_delivered) {
        throw OrderCannotBeFinishedException::notAllArticlesDelivered($order);
    }
    
    $order->update(['is_finished' => true]);
}
```

### Log Important Events
```php
// ✅ CORRECT - Log business events
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Log;

public function finishOrder(Order $order): void
{
    Log::info('Finishing order', [
        'order_id' => $order->id,
        'number' => $order->number,
        'user_id' => auth()->id(),
    ]);
    
    // ... finish order logic
    
    Log::info('Order finished successfully', [
        'order_id' => $order->id,
    ]);
}
```

