## 14. Git Commit Standards

### Use Conventional Commits
```bash
# Format: <type>(<scope>): <subject>

✅ CORRECT:
feat(orders): add montage time calculation
fix(tenancy): resolve database switching bug
refactor(services): extract financial logic to service
test(orders): add debt calculation tests
docs(readme): update installation instructions

❌ WRONG:
fixed bug
updates
wip
changes
```

### Atomic Commits
```bash
# ✅ CORRECT - One logical change per commit
git commit -m "feat(orders): add debt calculation accessor"
git commit -m "test(orders): add tests for debt calculation"
git commit -m "refactor(orders): move financial logic to service"

# ❌ WRONG - Multiple unrelated changes
git commit -m "add features and fix bugs"
```

